  {
   "key": "krea_v2_t2i",
   "label": "🔶 Krea2 V2",
   "headline": "A second artist, with a different eye.",
   "body": [
    "Some days you want the photographer. Some days you want the art director who actually reads the brief. This is the second one: give it a paragraph and it keeps every detail in it — the count, the placement, the colour of the third thing on the left — where a shorter attention span quietly drops half of them.",
    "It's also the one to reach for when there are words in the picture. Signage, packaging, a title on a poster: it writes them legibly, instead of producing something that only looks like text from across the room. Slower per image, and worth it when the brief is specific."
   ],
   "highlights": [
    "Follows long, detailed briefs",
    "Readable text in the image",
    "Holds composition instructions",
    "Made for the fussy shot"
   ],
