  {
   "key": "krea_v2_edit",
   "label": "🔷 Krea2 V2 Edit",
   "headline": "The same trick, for the fussier requests.",
   "body": [
    "Everything the Edit tab does, with a longer attention span. Ask for two changes at once — “move him to a studio backdrop and warm up the light” — and it does both, instead of doing the first and quietly averaging away the second.",
    "It's also gentler on the detail that repeated editing tends to sand off: hair, jewellery, the pattern on a shirt. Reach for it when the instruction is a sentence rather than a phrase, or when the picture has already been through a few rounds."
   ],
   "highlights": [
    "Two changes in one instruction",
    "Keeps fine detail intact",
    "Better after several rounds",
    "Same simple workflow"
   ],
